--- body ---

## Context

Child of 0700. The metadata profile of ticket 2043 (DataCite mandatory fields) requires a resource type. On the rebuilt pool of 389,291 works (the 2026-10-01 baseline) 32,744 works have a blank `doc_type`. Measured 2026-10-09:
- 32,084 are works with a catalogue row; 30,489 of the blank ones come from the catalogue's `openalex` source, the rest from other sources (teaching 452, istex 339, unfccc 227, bibcnrs 210, scispace 177, grey 149) and 660 are lane-only.
- 24,058 carry a DOI, 7,498 carry only an OpenAlex id, 1,188 carry neither.
- The vocabulary already in the pool (by count): journal-article 204,458; article 108,705; working-paper 16,055; book-chapter 6,273; preprint 3,926; conference-paper 2,831; dissertation 2,642; book 1,972; report 1,733; plus platform strings such as Electronic Resource 1,699 and Academic Journal 1,473.

The pinned catalogue (`data/catalogs/unified_works_rel_pin.csv`, md5 3633ad9f…) is never regenerated by REL: the repair has to come as a lane delivery or as an enrichment table the pool build joins. Pool metadata take each field from the first non-empty member, catalogue first, so a lane member carrying a type fills the blank.

Expected route (not measured): OpenAlex `type` by id batch (`filter=ids.openalex`, 100 ids per call, measured 0.0001 USD per call: about 316 calls for 31,556 works with an id, about USD 0.03, derived), Crossref `type` by DOI as a fallback for works OpenAlex does not return. The backfill of ticket 2041 does not carry `type` (its select is authorships, primary_location, locations), so this is a second, small fetch. The 1,188 works with no identifier cannot be recovered this way.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The recovery route is chosen and justified from a probe on a stratified sample of the blank works (by catalogue source and period), with the hit rate per route; no live call beyond that probe before the cost is shown to the author. The OpenAlex budget is shared (1 USD per day); the metering of `scripts/_rel_meter.py` is reused.
- [ ] The recovered type maps into the pool's existing doc_type vocabulary (stated mapping table; unknown values kept and counted, never invented); where OpenAlex and Crossref disagree the rule is stated.
- [ ] Delivery without changing any `work_key`: a lane delivery under the intake contract (records keyed by DOI or OpenAlex id carrying `doc_type`) or an enrichment table the pool build joins; the choice is stated with its reason. Fill blank only: no non-blank delivered value is overwritten.
- [ ] Pool check on the same inputs before and after: the set of `work_key` is identical and every pool column except `doc_type` is byte-identical; the count of works whose `doc_type` changes equals the count delivered.
- [ ] Counts by lane, period (1990-2006, 2007-2014, 2015-2025) and language: blank before and after; the residue (no identifier, or no answer) is listed; the effect on the 2043 profile (works excluded for resource type, before and after) is attached to the 2043 ticket log.
- [ ] Diff at most 14 content-bearing paths; scoped gate quoted (`selected:` and `skipped:`).

## Notes

Severity: science lane (a harvest gap that would exclude 32,744 works from the filter, 8.4% of the pool). Blocks switching the 2043 profile on, not its merge: the profile ships off. Related: 2049 (regenerate the partial lane deliveries), which can carry this if both lanes of work are sequenced together; keep the PRs separate.
